WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.307
This gate supports NIST special publication
eight hundred fifty-three A C two,

3
00:00:06.307 --> 00:00:08.629
which asks you to authorize access on

4
00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:12.225
organization-defined attributes
and to review accounts.

5
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:18.037
It supports A C six, least privilege,
and A C five, separation of duties.

6
00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:23.551
It supports P S five, personnel transfer,
which is what the residual review is for.

7
00:00:23.551 --> 00:00:28.522
And it supports scuba policy seven
point five, highly privileged roles only

8
00:00:28.522 --> 00:00:34.125
through a privileged access management
system, required under BOD 25-01.

9
00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:38.300
Your organization still sets the
organization-defined parameters,

10
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.450
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.

11
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:46.473
The evidence an ISSO keeps for
Gate 4: the reviewed policy files,

12
00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:50.337
the lint's clean run, and
the hash of each body sent.

13
00:00:50.337 --> 00:00:53.137
The member-of scan's
output with zero rows.

14
00:00:53.137 --> 00:00:54.926
A A oh nine's clean run.

15
00:00:54.926 --> 00:00:56.674
Each mover's residual sheet,

16
00:00:56.674 --> 00:01:00.475
the manager's decisions and the
transfer-to-review interval.

17
00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:04.390
And the separation-of-duties settings
in the package configuration.
